================================================================================
 STAGE B (cont).  The coarse-grained worldline EFT, derived, vs AeST eq (5)
================================================================================

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 B.1  THE Y^{3/2} TEST (D3).  Does deep-MOND MI coarse-grain to AeST's Y^{3/2}?
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AeST deep-MOND (CITED, 2007.00082): the scalar self-action density is
   L_phi^{dMOND} = - (1/16pi Gt) F(Y,Q0)   with   F -> (2-K_B) J(Y),
   J(Y) -> (2 lambda_s / (3(1+lambda_s) a0)) Y^{3/2},    Y = |grad phi|^2  (quasistatic).
So the AeST scalar Lagrangian density in deep MOND is  L ~ - (const/a0) |grad phi|^3.

Now derive the coarse-grained worldline side. The MI force law on ONE worldline in deep
MOND is  m mu_fw(a/a0) a = F  with mu_fw -> a/a0, i.e.  F = m a^2/a0 (the deep-MOND inertia).
Coarse-grain a CONGRUENCE: let phi(x) be the collective potential with the matter coupling
phi*rho (universal, as in AeST eq 2/6) and the test acceleration a = |grad phi| (a particle
in the field reads acceleration = gradient of the potential). The COLLECTIVE action whose
variation reproduces the single-worldline deep-MOND law is the AQUAL functional (Bekenstein-
Milgrom 1984; AeST eq 1):
   div( |grad phi|/a0 * grad phi ) = 4 pi G rho
which is the Euler-Lagrange equation of
   L_AQUAL = - (1/(8 pi G)) * (2/3) (1/a0) |grad phi|^3  + phi rho.            (AQUAL Lagrangian)

  EL flux of  -(1/3)(1/a0)|grad phi|^3  ==  -(|grad phi|/a0) grad phi (the MOND flux): True
  => the AQUAL flux IS the MOND flux. The deep-MOND COLLECTIVE Lagrangian IS ~|grad phi|^3.
  AeST deep-MOND prefactor 2 lam_s/(3(1+lam_s)) -> 2/3 in the screening limit lam_s->inf;
  the POWER (Y^{3/2}) and the 1/a0 SCALING are the convention-independent matched facts.

  AeST Y^{3/2} with Y=|grad phi|^2:  Y^{3/2} = (|grad phi|^2)^{3/2} = |grad phi|^3.  
  (|grad phi|^2)^{3/2} - |grad phi|^3  = 0  (0 => Y^{3/2}=|grad phi|^3 for Y=|grad phi|^2).

  RESULT B.1 (D3): the deep-MOND limit of the coarse-grained MI law IS the |grad phi|^3 = Y^{3/2}
  term of AeST, WITH a0 entering exactly where AeST puts it (the 1/a0 coefficient).
  *** MATCH (structural + scaling), and it is the strongest single piece of the join. ***
  CAVEAT (honest): this match is the well-known fact that BOTH theories reduce to AQUAL/BM84
  in deep MOND. It shows the IR fixed point coincides; it does NOT by itself show the UV
  completions coincide. The |grad phi|^3 is the SHARED deep-MOND attractor, not unique to AeST.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 B.2  FIELD CONTENT (D1: aether=u^mu, D2: scalar=collective MI field)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The worldline MI action reads accelerations IN A PREFERRED FRAME (the u-frame: the dS-bath
rest frame, where T_eff is isotropic). Coarse-graining a congruence with 4-velocity u^mu(x)
PRODUCES a unit-timelike vector field u^mu u_mu = -1 BY CONSTRUCTION (4-velocities are unit
timelike).
  (D1)  u^mu (coarse-grained, unit-timelike)  <->  AeST A^mu (unit-timelike, A^2=-1):
        *** STRUCTURAL MATCH ***  both are unit-timelike vectors; both select a preferred
        frame; both break local Lorentz invariance the SAME way (the MOND anisotropy
        |grad phi|^3 vs the cosmological phid^2,phid^4 -- AeST's own stated motivation, eq
        after (4): 'anisotropic scaling ... heuristically implies Lorentz violation ...
        introduced via a unit-timelike vector A_mu'). The framework's dS-bath frame is
        PHYSICALLY the same object AeST introduces phenomenologically. CREDIT.

  (D2)  the collective MI field phi: the worldline MI response is encoded in a potential whose
        gradient is the modified acceleration. Coarse-grained over the congruence this is a
        scalar field phi(x), shift-symmetric (only grad phi enters the force -- the MI law
        depends on acceleration = grad of potential, never on phi itself).
        AeST phi is ALSO shift-symmetric (eq 5: 'shift symmetric under phi->phi+phi0').
        *** STRUCTURAL MATCH on the symmetry ***. CREDIT.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 B.3  THE GAPS (both ways): which AeST terms does the worldline coarse-graining
      FAIL to produce / cannot fix?
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AeST eq (5):  R - (K_B/2)F^2 + 2(2-K_B) J.grad phi - (2-K_B) Y - F(Y,Q) - lambda(A^2+1).
Go term by term and ask: does worldline MI coarse-graining FORCE it, with its coefficient?

  [R]            : Einstein-Hilbert. The worldline MI action is on a FIXED (weak-field) metric;
                   coarse-graining test bodies does NOT generate the gravitational R term --
                   that is the host gravity, put in separately. (Expected: R is gravity, not MI.)
                   STATUS: not produced by MI; supplied by the host. OK but not a 'derivation'.

  [-(K_B/2)F^2]  : the aether KINETIC term (Maxwell-like, F=2 grad_[mu A_nu]).
                   *** THE FIRST HARD GAP ***. Coarse-grained worldline 4-velocities u^mu give a
                   unit-timelike FIELD, but its DYNAMICS (the kinetic term that makes A^mu a
                   propagating d.o.f. with coefficient K_B) is NOT fixed by the MI worldline
                   action. The MI action uses u^mu as a BACKGROUND clock/frame (it READS
                   accelerations in it); it does not give u^mu its own Maxwell kinetic action.
                   K_B is a FREE AeST parameter; nothing in the MI coarse-graining selects it.
                   STATUS: GAP. The aether kinetic sector is ASSUMED, not derived.

  [2(2-K_B)J.grad phi] : the J^mu grad_mu phi MIXING term, J^mu = A^a grad_a A^mu (the aether
                   ACCELERATION dotted into grad phi). This term couples the aether's own
                   acceleration to the scalar gradient. In the worldline picture J^mu = u-frame
                   acceleration of the congruence; grad phi = MI response. So a coupling
                   (congruence acceleration).(MI response) IS natural from MI coarse-graining
                   (the MI force IS the response to acceleration).
                   STATUS: PLAUSIBLE structural origin, but the COEFFICIENT 2(2-K_B) is tied to
                   K_B (the un-derived kinetic coeff) -- so even this 'natural' term inherits the
                   gap. PARTIAL.

  [-(2-K_B)Y - F(Y,Q)] : Y = orthogonal |grad phi|^2, Q = A.grad phi. The Y and F(Y,Q) terms are
                   the scalar self-action whose deep-MOND limit is the Y^{3/2} (B.1 MATCH). The
                   FULL function F(Y,Q) is FREE in AeST (a free function!) -- so the worldline
                   kernel coarse-grains to SOME F(Y,Q); AeST does not constrain it either, so
                   there is nothing to fail against here EXCEPT the deep-MOND limit (matched B.1).
                   STATUS: deep-MOND limit MATCH (B.1); full F free on both sides (no constraint).

  [-lambda(A^2+1)] : the unit constraint. Automatic from u^mu being a 4-velocity (u^2=-1).
                   STATUS: MATCH (trivial -- both impose unit-timelike).

